---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Application privacy">
  <article class="prose-precision">
    <h1 class="text-display-lg font-bold">Application privacy</h1>
    <p>
      We collect your LinkedIn account identifier, name, available email, and
      the background and project details you submit to assess membership in the
      GenerativeAI Community.
    </p>
    <h2>How assessment works</h2>
    <p>
      A Cloudflare-hosted AI assessment checks whether your application
      describes concrete work building, researching, or applying AI. Clear
      matches can be approved automatically. Uncertain applications go to a
      community administrator. We treat the background you provide as
      self-reported.
    </p>
    <h2>Your information</h2>
    <p>
      Application information and decision records are stored on Cloudflare and
      are accessible to community administrators. We send verification and
      invitation emails using Cloudflare Email Service. Information is used to
      administer membership, handle support requests, and prevent duplicate or
      abusive applications.
    </p>
    <h2>Using an agent</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to share an application token with Codex or another agent,
      that agent can read the application details and submit one application on
      your behalf for 24 hours. You can revoke or replace the token on your
      application page. Your agent provider’s own data policies also apply.
    </p>
    <h2>Requests and corrections</h2>
    <p>
      For access, correction, or deletion requests, contact{" "}
      <a href="mailto:nirant@scaledfocus.com">nirant@scaledfocus.com</a>.
      Application data is retained while needed to administer your application
      or membership; you can request deletion. Avoid submitting confidential
      employer information or personal data about other people.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
